<section class="pgt-reading" aria-labelledby="up-pgt-about">
  <h2 id="up-pgt-about">About UP PGT English</h2>
  <p><strong>UP PGT</strong> is the Uttar Pradesh Post Graduate Teacher recruitment conducted by the Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (<strong>UPESSC</strong>).</p>
  <p>PGT stands for <strong>Post Graduate Teacher</strong>. A PGT teaches English at the senior secondary level — Classes XI and XII.</p>
  <p>Use this general English study guide to plan your reading and revision. It is not an official UP PGT syllabus. Check the current UPESSC notification for the required qualifications, eligibility conditions, exam pattern, marking and prescribed texts.</p>
</section>

<section class="pgt-reading" aria-labelledby="up-pgt-study">
  <h2 id="up-pgt-study">English study areas</h2>
  <p>Match these broad English study areas to the official syllabus for the recruitment you are taking.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Study area</th><th scope="col">What to revise</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Reading Comprehension</th><td>Unseen prose, poetry and factual passages. Inference, tone, vocabulary and summarising.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Writing Skills</th><td>Letters, notices, reports, articles, speeches and debates.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Applied Grammar</th><td>Tenses, voice, narration, transformation, prepositions, agreement, punctuation, idioms and phrases.</td></tr>
